%N A147535 a(n) = 2*4^n + 4*3^n - 2^n.
%H A147535 Harvey P. Dale, <a href="/A147535/b147535.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A147535 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (9,-26,24).
%F A147535 From _R. J. Mathar_, Nov 09 2008: (Start)
%F A147535 a(n) = 9*a(n-1)-26*a(n-2)+24*a(n-3) = 2*4^n+4*3^n-2^n.
%F A147535 G.f.: (5-27*x+32*x^2)/((1-2*x)*(1-3*x)*(1-4*x)). (End)
%F A147535 E.g.f.: exp(2*x)*(2*exp(2*x) + 4*exp(x) - 1). - _Stefano Spezia_, Oct 18 2026
